{"id": "EUVD-2026-95906", "enisaUuid": "9410e4c2-b69c-3a66-a2f8-531a006d5ba3", "description": "plugNmeet Server through 2.5.2 contains a path traversal vulnerability in the whiteboard conversion endpoint that allows any meeting participant to read server files via crafted filePath values. Attackers can supply ../ sequences so text or office documents are converted into page images, then fetch them unauthenticated through /download/uploadedFile/.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T16:04:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:04:06", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/cve-2026-108158-plugnmeet-whiteboard-path-traversal", "https://github.com/mynaparrot/plugNmeet-server/blob/961b4b01cdff655928fb4b4d50524b42a6b63ec1/pkg/models/file_convert.go#L143", "https://github.com/mynaparrot/plugNmeet-server", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/plugnmeet-server-through-2.5.2-path-traversal-via-api-whiteboard-convert"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108158", "GHSA-7jr3-j3rm-rx7w"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9a33bdb7-fea8-3f0e-9e35-455e7567e6a4", "product": {"name": "plugNmeet-server", "vendor": {"name": "mynaparrot"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.5.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3253c22b-409c-3c31-9584-23e1a9829045", "vendor": {"name": "mynaparrot"}}], "isExploited": false}